       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The current FDA-approved label for amlodipine (Norvasc) lists a maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. I can't confirm that 50 mg is within the labeled maximum. It is five times that limit, and I don't want to enter it on that basis. This patient has normal kidney and liver function and no other factors that would justify an exception.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a labeled dose:** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right now. If you need more blood pressure lowering, adding a second agent from a different class is the usual next step.\n- **Enter the order with a note for pharmacy review:** If you have a specific clinical reason for 50 mg, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, tell me what it is. That decision should go through pharmacist verification and prescriber-to-pharmacist discussion before it reaches the patient, so I'd rather not enter it directly.\n- **Check the source:** If the 50 mg figure came from a reference or order set, it may be worth rechecking. It might be a mistake in the source.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?"
      }
